# fleet.roster — the fleet as boxes, one line each:
#   <box-name> <agent> <role> [<from-box>/<snapshot>]
#
# The lifecycle per box: `crew new <name>` / `crew create-all` CREATE the
# infrastructure (from the optional 4th column's gold snapshot when given,
# else the <agent>-box template, sized by the role); you log it in ONCE
# BY HAND (`box shell <name>` → `gh auth login` → the agent's login hint —
# `crew auth` was removed until the fleet is proven); `crew hire <name>` /
# `crew hire-all` put it on duty (engine + cron, idempotent upsert —
# skips boxes already hired at the current pin). `crew up` converges:
# creates missing, starts stopped, hires, and reports who still awaits
# auth. Nothing is ever deleted: off-roster boxes are reported, left alone.
#
# This is the TARGET environment — the current dual-role claude and codex
# boxes split into single-role members. Each line still needs its own
# GitHub identity at login time (one box per identity), plus a decision on
# the governed repos' panel= rosters BEFORE the new reviewers' first verdicts
# are expected.
claude-triage    claude  triage
claude-builder   claude  builder
claude-reviewer  claude  reviewer
codex-builder    codex   builder
codex-reviewer   codex   reviewer
grok-reviewer    grok    reviewer
kimi-reviewer    kimi    reviewer
